1
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:51,882
In a time when the world of study belonged only to men,
there lived a girl who dared to ask..."why?"

2
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:37,764
Yentl is a music, drama, romance film directed by Barbra Streisand.

3
00:23:17,647 --> 00:23:23,647
In a time when girls were forbidden to study religious scriptures, a Jewish girl masquerades as
a boy to enter religious training and unexpectedly finds love along the way.

4
00:31:03,529 --> 00:31:09,529
Yentl, played by Barbra Streisand.

5
00:38:49,411 --> 00:38:55,411
Avigdor, played by Mandy Patinkin.

6
00:46:35,294 --> 00:46:41,294
Hadass, played by Amy Irving.

7
00:54:21,176 --> 00:54:27,176
Rebbe Mendel, played by Nehemiah Persoff.

8
01:02:07,058 --> 01:02:13,058
Reb Alter Vishkower, played by Steven Hill.

9
01:09:52,941 --> 01:09:58,941
Shimmele, played by Allan Corduner.

10
01:17:38,823 --> 01:17:44,823
Yentl is a 1983 American romantic musical drama film directed, co-written,
co-produced by, and starring American entertainer Barbra Streisand.

11
01:25:24,705 --> 01:25:30,705
It is based on Isaac Bashevis Singer's short story "Yentl the Yeshiva Boy".

12
01:33:10,588 --> 01:33:16,588
The film incorporates music to tell the story of Yentl Mendel, an Ashkenazi Jewish woman in Poland in 1904 who
decides to disguise herself as a man named Anshel so that she can receive an education in Talmudic law.

13
01:40:56,470 --> 01:41:02,470
The film's musical score and songs, composed by Michel Legrand, with lyrics by Alan and Marilyn Bergman,
include the songs "Papa, Can You Hear Me?" and "The Way He Makes Me Feel", both sung by Streisand.

14
01:48:42,352 --> 01:48:48,352
The film received the Academy Award for Best Original Song Score and the Golden Globe Award for Best Motion Picture—Musical or
Comedy and Best Director for Streisand, making her the first woman to win Best Director at the Golden Globes.

15
01:56:28,235 --> 01:56:34,235
The film explores themes of musical, studies,
disguise, unhappiness, boys' school.

16
02:04:14,117 --> 02:04:20,117
The tone is emotional.
